 Lean statement that implies the printed one. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.thm-mobius-lambert-identity"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.thm-mobius-lambert-identity"],"id":"long.thm-mobius-lambert-identity","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.28 (The Lambert-series identity for the Möbius function)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.28, p. 52, label thm:mobius-lambert-identity","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*The absolutely convergent signed series satisfies\n$$\n\\sum_{d\\ge1}\\frac{\\mu(d)}{2^d-1}=\\frac12.\n$$\nThis classical identity is also recorded in \\[duverneytachiya, Example 1.1, p. 4\\]. Expand each denominator geometrically and interchange the absolutely convergent sums. The coefficient of $2^{-n}$ is $\\sum_{d\\mid n}\\mu(d)$, equal to $1$ for $n=1$ and $0$ otherwise. This proves the identity. Its coefficients are $-1,0,1$, not indicators of a support; the identity therefore does not represent $1/2$ as a subseries with all coefficients in $\\{0,1\\}$.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.thm-mobius-lambert-identity","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.thm-mobius-lambert-identity","id":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.thm-mobius-lambert-identity%22%2C%22lean.MersenneLambertLadder.tsum_moebius_div_two_pow_sub_one_eq_half%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.thm-mobius-lambert-identity%22%2C%22lean.MersenneLambertLadder.tsum_moebius_div_two_pow_sub_one_eq_half%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/lean.MersenneLa